HST Constraint Integration Strategy

Determined that observational constraints should be applied at the galaxy center-of-mass level, not per particle.

Selected HST-aligned parameters:

Initial separation: ~780 kpc

Relative velocity vector: (−109, +20, 0) km/s

Designed a workflow where:

Galaxies are generated independently

Actual COMs are measured numerically

A global shift is applied to M31 particles only

Outcome: Observations constrain initial conditions without overfitting the microphysics.

